                      A Warrior Without Enemies           By: subhaan
-----------------------------------------------------------

Leif was known as the greatest fighter in the northern lands. He won every duel and earned endless fame.
One day, he met an old farmer who had never held a sword. The farmer lived peacefully and helped everyone around him.
Leif realized that despite all his victories, he was never truly at peace.
He laid down his weapon and began building homes instead of destroying them.
Years later, people remembered him not for the battles he won, but for the lives he improved.
The greatest victory is conquering hatred.
